2186045417] [17592186299237 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186297674 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299237 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b0d77a70-66b2-5ffc-82b6-2ce4bec2f8bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299378 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186298183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299378 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299378 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299378 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186298183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299378 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d9818ff9-bf1d-504a-a640-f403039467ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299747 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299747 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299237 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299747 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299747 #edb/ref 1069 "q-319360" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299747 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299747 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}]$\ngiven that $det(A)=-5.$\n\n|  |  | $-17$ | {{field-1}} | $-1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\,$ |  | $12$ | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |\n|  |  | $-3$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299747 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0876fd99-09ab-5402-abb3-c07e19b050b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299747 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-17 & -12 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-17 & 12 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-17 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-17 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 12 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299778 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299778 #edb/ref 1069 "q-319550" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299778 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299778 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nif its determinant is $-22.$\n\n${a}_{33}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299778 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "959ebdb0-727b-5193-9194-4f73c8f717da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299778 #edb/ref 1074 "Since we want the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{33}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{33} & =(-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\,1\\cdot (2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{33}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\,{c}_{33} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-22}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299812 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299812 #edb/ref 1069 "q-319944" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299812 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299812 #edb/ref 1071 "The entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ k & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nequals $-2.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299812 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "44f3f3e2-3340-514f-8bf3-b71afd4ac18e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186299812 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ k & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ k & -1\\end{aligned}|+(-2)|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ k & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)((-1)(-1)-(-2)(-2))+2((-2)(-1)-(-2)k)+(-2)((-2)(-2)-(-1)k) \\\\  & =(-2)(1-4)+2(2+2k)+(-2)(4+k) \\\\  & =6+4+4k-8-2k \\\\  & =2k+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{32}^{t}={c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ k & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-((-2)(-2)-(-2)k) \\\\  & =-(4+2k) \\\\  & =-2k-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{32}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2k-4}{2k+2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{k+2}{k+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{32}^{′}=-2$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{k+2}{k+1} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{k+2}{k+1} & =2 \\\\ k+2 & =2k+2 \\\\ k & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426296 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426296 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426296 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "16cc7665-faef-5318-96fb-c89a1b7adc64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426297 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426297 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426297 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "332694ea-bd99-5523-b1d8-48a224b3dc34" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426298 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426298 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426298 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "39a3852a-5680-51e4-9e2a-405e8aa0a909" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426299 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426299 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426299 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6ed8db16-e8bd-5c83-b560-aef74fb47014" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426300 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426300 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426300 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "864823ca-9fd6-5647-872e-3574bd6be0c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426301 #edb/ref 1080 "-3[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426301 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426301 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "95310ad0-4ea0-549a-b41e-47e2e1481ffb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426302 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1\