ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426303 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426307 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186426304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426307 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426307 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426307 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186426300 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426307 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7ea44ec1-58ba-5956-a980-aec4c772ced8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426308 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426307 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426308 #edb/ref 1069 "q-104435" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426308 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426308 #edb/ref 1071 "The entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & k & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $2.$ Find the value of $k.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426308 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "60094f6c-d2bd-58df-8627-15176f255263" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426308 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & k & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-k-6)-0+1(6-k) \\\\  & =-k-6+6-k \\\\  & =-2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-2-2) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2k}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{21}^{′}=2$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{k} & =2 \\\\ -2 & =2k \\\\ -\\frac{2}{2} & =k \\\\ k & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426309 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426306 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426309 #edb/ref 1069 "q-73478" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426309 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426309 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\ngiven that $det(A)=-3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426309 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ccf4f432-0d42-54bc-b36a-bd39fd754033" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426309 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -8 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
